---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import DonateForm from "@/components/DonateForm";
import { ALL, CATALOGUE_UPDATED, COMPANIES, DOCUMENTED_COUNT, FIRST_YEAR, LAST_YEAR } from "@/data/collection";
---

<Layout title="Curator's note — Merchback Machine" compact={true}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8">
    <div class="border-b-2 border-ink pb-3">
      <p class="meta">About this archive</p>
      <h2 class="mt-1 font-display text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Curator's note</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Merch is the only artifact most companies produce that outlives their product. The code gets
        rewritten, the domain gets parked, and the shirt stays in somebody's drawer for fifteen years.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>{ALL.length} objects</strong> from <strong>{COMPANIES.length} companies</strong>,{" "}
        {FIRST_YEAR}–{LAST_YEAR}: tees, caps, socks, stickers, pins, plushies, keycaps, a hardcover, a
        fedora, and a few things that fit no category at all.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-10 border-b border-ink pb-1 font-display text-lg font-bold">On dating</h3>
      <p>
        {DOCUMENTED_COUNT} of {ALL.length} records carry a documented year. The rest are marked{" "}
        <span class="acc">≈</span> — anchored to the product or campaign era, not a verified production
        run. Nobody files a press release about a sock. If you can date one properly, the registrar
        wants to hear it.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-10 border-b border-ink pb-1 font-display text-lg font-bold">On the plates</h3>
      <p>
        Every object is a drawn <em>specimen plate</em> in the recorded colorway, not a photograph.
        The archive holds no photography rights, and a drawing is honest about being an interpretation.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-10 border-b border-ink pb-1 font-display text-lg font-bold">On scarcity</h3>
      <p>
        “Widely distributed” through “grail” indexes how hard a piece is to find today. It isn't an
        appraisal: nothing here is for sale and nothing here is valued.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section id="donate" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-6">
      <div class="border-b-2 border-ink pb-3">
        <p class="stamp">accession desk</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Donate an artifact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Describe the object and it joins the accession queue. Corrections welcome too — name the
          accession number in the record field.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6">
        <DonateForm client:load />
      </div>
      <p class="meta mt-4">Catalogue revision {CATALOGUE_UPDATED}</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
